    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/premiseText> "(1) This clause applies to a draft variation of a final operational separation plan unless:  (a) the draft variation was given to the Minister as a result of a direction under subclause 56A(2); or  (b) both:  (i) Telstra had previously given the Minister a written outline of the draft variation; and  (ii) the Minister, by written notice given to Telstra, had informed Telstra that the Minister was satisfied that the draft variation was of a minor nature.";
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/conclusionText> "(1) This clause applies to a draft variation of a final operational separation plan unless:  (a) the draft variation was given to the Minister as a result of a direction under subclause 56A(2); or  (b) both:  (i) Telstra had previously given the Minister a written outline of the draft variation; and  (ii) the Minister, by written notice given to Telstra, had informed Telstra that the Minister was satisfied that the draft variation was of a minor nature.";
